<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'AWS VPC Networking & Security'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>AWS VPC Networking & Security Architecture</h1>
  <p>Full VPC with public/private subnets, IGW, NAT Gateway, bastion host, custom NACLs, and SSH tunneling validation.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>VPC</span><span>Subnets</span><span>NAT Gateway</span><span>NACL</span><span>Bastion Host</span><span>Security Groups</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/vpc-networking.png" alt="VPC Networking Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates building a <strong>production-ready VPC architecture</strong> with network segmentation, secure access patterns, and defense-in-depth security controls.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created a <strong>VPC</strong> with custom CIDR block (10.0.0.0/16).</li>
      <li>Built <strong>public and private subnets</strong> for network segmentation.</li>
      <li>Attached <strong>Internet Gateway</strong> for public internet access.</li>
      <li>Deployed <strong>NAT Gateway</strong> for secure private subnet outbound access.</li>
      <li>Set up <strong>bastion host</strong> architecture with SSH agent forwarding.</li>
      <li>Created <strong>custom NACLs</strong> and tested ICMP blocking.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🌐 Network Design</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>VPC</strong> — 10.0.0.0/16</li>
          <li><strong>Public Subnet</strong> — 10.0.0.0/24</li>
          <li><strong>Private Subnet</strong> — 10.0.1.0/24</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔀 Traffic Routing</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>IGW</strong> — Public subnet → Internet</li>
          <li><strong>NAT Gateway</strong> — Private subnet → Internet</li>
          <li>Separate route tables per subnet</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔒 Security Layers</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Bastion Host</strong> — SSH jump box</li>
          <li><strong>Custom NACLs</strong> — Subnet-level firewall</li>
          <li><strong>Security Groups</strong> — Instance-level rules</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created <strong>Lab VPC</strong> (10.0.0.0/16), public and private subnets.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Attached <strong>Internet Gateway</strong> and created public route table (0.0.0.0/0 → IGW).</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Created <strong>NAT Gateway</strong> with Elastic IP, created private route table.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Launched <strong>bastion host</strong> (public) and private EC2 instance.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Tested SSH via bastion with <strong>agent forwarding</strong>, verified NAT with ping.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">6</div><p>Created <strong>custom NACL</strong> and tested ICMP blocking on private subnet.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Designed <strong>public vs private subnet</strong> architecture with proper routing.</li>
      <li>Deployed <strong>NAT Gateway</strong> for secure outbound-only access.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>bastion host</strong> pattern with SSH agent forwarding.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>NACLs</strong> for subnet-level traffic control alongside Security Groups.</li>
      <li>Practiced <strong>defense in depth</strong> — multiple security layers.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

